WEBVTT

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:13.420
Please fight with me, Kaito.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.180
Upperclassman! Your eye!

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:21.020
Ah, has its color changed?

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:24.420
It's all right. I haven't changed at all.

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:29.390
This is an important experiment.
And a challenge, too.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:31.940
Will you help me?

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:33.820
Kaito...

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:52.920
Lost

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:56.840
Tesaguri de sagashiteta
I've searched, groping

00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:59.800
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
The answer to a future that's been closed off

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:01.760
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
Is nowhere to be found

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.180
Hashiru shoudou, ima kaidoku funou
The impulse to run, it's impossible to decipher now

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:06.600
Found

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:11.110
Kudaketa hazu no unmei o
A fate that was supposedly smashed

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:15.610
Mijuku na yume no naka de kikoeta kitanda
I've come to hear it within that half-formed dream:

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:18.200
Saigo made I'll be there for you
Until the end, I'll be there for you

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:21.580
Tachidomaranai, kono hari dake wa
It won't stop, not this needle

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:24.870
Boku no asu o kizamu oto o tsukisasu
It will pierce the sound that engraves my tomorrow

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:26.580
Shinjitsu kara nigetara ima
If I run from the truth, then now...

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:28.420
Genjitsu ni mo maketara ima
If I lose to reality, then now...

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:30.790
Nani ga nokoru no?
What will remain?

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.000
(Nokoru no?)
(Will remain?)

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.460
Kazoekirenai kono kizu dake ga
These countless wounds of mine

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:38.800
Boku no kinou o zanzou to shite kataru
They tell of my yesterday as an afterimage

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:40.430
Unmei ga hodoketemo ima
Even if fate were unraveled, now...

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:42.390
Sonzai o kowashitemo ima
Even if my existence were smashed, now...

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:45.270
Boku no michi o yuku yo
I will travel my path

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:47.060
It's now or never

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:48.600
That is what they say

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.600
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:53.820
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:55.440
That is what they say

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:57.440
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:00.740
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:02.450
That is what they say

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:04.870
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:11.000
Forbidden Fruit

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:21.510
This is friggin' heavy!

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:24.120
Oh, dear. Thanks for your hard work.

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:27.270
The heck is this thing?!

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:31.560
"SJ"?

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:34.130
Sliding Junction.

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:38.300
A special puzzle I made
for my graduation project.

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:41.200
Why'd we have to bring it to the roof?

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:44.180
This is my special seat.

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:48.430
I thought this would be best
for doing a puzzle with you.

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:58.670
This may be the last puzzle.

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:08.350
Kaito, will you help me set it up?

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:19.470
It's like...

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:22.610
Upperclassman Jikukawa
seems the same as always, huh?

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:26.950
His brain is definitely in
an activate state. But...

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:29.580
Souji hasn't changed.

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:32.810
Is that Ring broken?

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:38.040
No. Upperclassman Jikukawa is
suppressing the Ring's power.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:41.900
There's no way one of their
fakes could swallow me up.

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:44.840
If anything, I will control IT.

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:50.240
A normal person would
have lost control by now.

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:52.670
Upperclassman Jikukawa is incredible!

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:57.170
All right, now it's complete.

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:05.550
This is... SJ.

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:11.120
Oh, my. I almost forgot.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.850
What is that?

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:15.370
A bomb.

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:19.510
I made it so that I can control something

00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:21.800
of the Orpheus Order's making.

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:26.060
When the fuse burns
up, the bomb goes off.

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:30.110
Half of Root Gakuen will sink into the ground.

00:04:31.010 --> 00:04:34.760
If you win, Kaito, I'll tell
you the password to stop it.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:38.630
For real? You're saying this for real?

00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:41.210
So that you treat this
with due importance.

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:45.590
Otherwise, you won't know the power of this Ring.

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:47.490
I told you, didn't I?

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:51.790
This is an important
experiment, and a challenge.

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:54.290
Still, a bomb is just-

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:55.610
Upperclassman Jikukawa.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:05:00.880
The truth is, that Ring already
swallowed you up, ain't it?

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:06.990
There's no way that could be!
Upperclassman Jikukawa...

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:10.800
Upperclassman Jikukawa
wouldn't be beaten by the Ring!

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:14.000
The bomb is just to get Kaito motivated!

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:18.060
That... That's right...

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:20.230
Cube.

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:23.610
That's right, right?
Upperclassman Jikukawa!

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:30.660
We know more than anyone
how dangerous those Rings are.

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:32.950
Fine, then I'll go take a look!

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:38.160
If there's a bomb, I'll
dismantle it myself!

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:40.560
But if there isn't one...

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:43.750
You better kowtow before
Upperclassman Jikukawa!

00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:47.970
Cubik...

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:50.530
Nonoha. Ana.

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:54.330
Hurry up and get the students
still at the academy to go home.

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:55.770
Huh?

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:56.330
Wha-?

00:05:57.730 --> 00:05:59.830
Just in case.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:02.730
Let's go, Nonoha.

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:06.230
Hey! Wait! Ana!

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:11.950
I'll stay and keep an eye on ya.

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:13.950
After all, there's a kowtow involved.

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:18.020
Are you all ready, Kaito?

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:20.400
Yeah. I'm good.

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:23.880
Puzzle time... Let's begin.

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:33.180
Sliding Junction...

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:37.520
You move red and blue trains
on same-colored rails,

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:41.190
heading for the opponents' station
in a competitive sliding puzzle, huh?

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:45.420
In the Solver's turn, you slide two rails

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:48.170
while the train proceeds two blocks.

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:55.580
Slide three rail blocks and
the train will advance one block.

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:59.100
In the Giver's turn, you use the

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:01.600
handheld panel to select new blocks.

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:04.570
Those blocks appear above the field.

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:07.040
Once arranged, they create new rails.

00:07:08.550 --> 00:07:12.950
On either turn, you can't move the block
on which the train moves.

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:16.140
It's time to switch turns. Kaito.

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:17.760
Yeah.

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:21.860
A one-on-one puzzle, with
Giver and Solver switching places...

00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:25.630
That's pretty friggin' fun,
Upperclassman Jikukawa!

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:36.420
That's right.

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:41.100
No one knows just how skilled
Upperclassman Jikukawa is.

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:44.000
Newton vs. Einstein, huh?

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:46.510
That bomb is buggin' me,

00:07:46.510 --> 00:07:48.610
but this is one battle
I can't take my eyes off of!

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:51.950
Time to switch turns,
Upperclassman Jikukawa.

00:07:52.590 --> 00:07:54.420
Well done, Kaito.

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:56.910
It helps that you've
learned the rules so quickly.

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:00.910
Is he...

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:04.420
Is he really the same
upperclassman as always?

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:10.940
Upperclassman Jikukawa
can't lose to that Replica Ring!

00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:18.140
Still, why would he fight with me

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:20.060
to the point of setting off a bomb?

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:22.560
If it's like Gammon says...

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:26.310
and he's been swallowed
up by the Ring...!

00:08:28.210 --> 00:08:29.130
All right!

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:32.960
Now, most of the rails
Upperclassman Jikukawa

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:34.960
could've used to move forward are gone.

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:39.240
What's more, his train is
ass-backward from the goal.

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:41.790
Comin' back from this will be pretty tough.

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:43.860
I'm surprised.

00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:45.790
Very well done, Kaito.

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:47.750
With that move just now,

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:49.800
you've made victory for
me rather difficult.

00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:52.290
But it's strange...

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:57.050
Somehow, I don't at all feel
like I'm going to lose.

00:08:57.990 --> 00:09:00.320
So we can speed things up a bit.

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:01.370
Huh?

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:03.540
How about this?

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:14.950
Hey! What the hell are you doing?!

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:17.070
You're changin' the rules?!

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:19.490
Just hurrying things up.

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:22.950
To meet our speed.

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:32.730
Ana! Any luck over there?

00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:34.920
Not a creature stirring,
not even a hamster!

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:42.530
Upperclassman Chieno!

00:09:42.530 --> 00:09:44.310
Oh, my. What's going on?

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:46.750
Let's go. It's dangerous!

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:49.460
Dangerous? What is?

00:09:49.460 --> 00:09:50.500
At the ruins in the mountain-

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:51.540
Nonoha!
At the ruins in the mountain-

00:09:55.210 --> 00:09:59.450
U-Um... Going home at night is dangerous!

00:10:00.930 --> 00:10:04.750
Sorry. I have to sort
through these documents

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:06.140
that piled up during the elections.

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:08.180
But, you don't have to do that now.

00:10:08.180 --> 00:10:09.160
That won't do!

00:10:09.890 --> 00:10:12.210
If I do my job slipshod like that,

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:15.170
it will be an insult to
Upperclassman Jikukawa.

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:17.240
Upperclassman Chieno...

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:19.490
I, Ana, will help.

00:10:20.570 --> 00:10:22.010
I'll help you, too!

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:24.900
Let's get it done soon and go home!

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:28.020
Thank you.

00:10:34.340 --> 00:10:36.550
It's my turn, as a Solver.

00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:44.660
He joined the friggin' rails!

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:57.210
It's your turn to be Solver.

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:07.470
I can see it.

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:18.250
I can see it... I can see it, Kaito.

00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:20.990
All the moves you're trying to make!

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:23.630
U-Upperclassman Jikukawa!

00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:27.120
This is... the power of the Ring, is it?

00:11:29.310 --> 00:11:30.770
His apple juice!

00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:31.710
He threw it down?!

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:36.360
Yes. It has no flavor at all.

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:39.390
Abandoning all senses and emotions,

00:11:39.390 --> 00:11:42.300
shifting all areas of the brain toward thought, eh?

00:11:42.950 --> 00:11:46.140
My, this is a surprising experience.

00:11:46.490 --> 00:11:50.450
Sir... Sure enough, you...!

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:55.220
It's all right. I'm all right.

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:06.010
Over there.

00:12:12.310 --> 00:12:14.640
It's my turn as a Solver.

00:12:19.110 --> 00:12:21.370
I can see it... I can see it!

00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:23.860
Dammit!

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:32.160
I can see it. Limitless moves!

00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:41.940
I can beat Kaito...

00:12:42.590 --> 00:12:45.260
A Phi-Brain child!

00:12:46.510 --> 00:12:48.850
This puzzle sure is fun.

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:54.440
We can enjoy bein' both Giver and Solver.

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:57.130
Nice one, Upperclassman Jikukawa!

00:12:57.980 --> 00:13:00.100
It's tough, but the more you

00:13:00.100 --> 00:13:02.340
think about it,
the more fun it gets.

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:05.060
For sure, I feel it...

00:13:05.060 --> 00:13:08.000
The thought you put into this puzzle.

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:13.120
"SJ." You even gave
this your own initials.

00:13:13.540 --> 00:13:16.310
Isn't that right, Souji Jikukawa?

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:20.900
I don't know what you're thinkin', but...

00:13:21.880 --> 00:13:23.780
I'm gonna enjoy this.

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:25.910
This puzzle is the best!

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:29.680
All finished!

00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:31.140
I, Ana, too!

00:13:31.350 --> 00:13:33.720
Okay, let's go home.

00:13:33.720 --> 00:13:35.430
H-Hey!

00:13:35.850 --> 00:13:37.540
Come on, come on!

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:39.810
Hang on a minute, Miss Itou!

00:13:39.810 --> 00:13:41.920
Come one, come on!

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:44.760
Here I go, Upperclassman Jikukawa!

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:52.700
I see it!

00:14:02.460 --> 00:14:05.320
That settles it. With this, Kaito wins!

00:14:10.260 --> 00:14:12.530
I've solved it, Upperclassman Jikukawa.

00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:18.810
Well, well. You're most talented, Kaito.

00:14:19.240 --> 00:14:20.040
But...

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:24.110
It's my turn as a Solver.

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:34.130
U-Upperclassman Jikukawa.

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:37.500
Our duel is already decided...

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:41.440
Just a little more, and
I might be able to reach it...

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:46.050
Phi-Brain level!

00:14:53.300 --> 00:14:55.750
What... am I doing?

00:15:39.770 --> 00:15:42.040
I lost, huh?

00:15:49.280 --> 00:15:51.180
Upperclassman Jikukawa! Hang in there!

00:15:51.190 --> 00:15:52.450
Hey!

00:15:53.490 --> 00:15:55.410
What about the bomb?!

00:15:56.570 --> 00:15:58.030
It's all right.

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:03.080
All the explosive mechanisms
have been disabled.

00:16:05.250 --> 00:16:07.610
Sure enough, this was part
of the upperclassman's plan.

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:08.910
All of it!

00:16:16.010 --> 00:16:18.220
Kaito
No problems with
the upperclassman
or the school

00:16:19.430 --> 00:16:21.520
Thank goodness!

00:16:21.770 --> 00:16:23.640
I, Ana, was so worried!

00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:25.140
Me, too!

00:16:26.150 --> 00:16:27.360
What...

00:16:28.360 --> 00:16:30.730
Now that I can relax, I'm SO hungry!

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:32.240
I, Ana, too!

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:34.230
Oh! Ma'am, shall we

00:16:34.230 --> 00:16:36.510
get something to eat
on the way back?

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:37.550
To celebrate.

00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:40.140
Celebrate? Celebrate what?

00:16:40.580 --> 00:16:41.740
Celebraaaate!

00:16:41.740 --> 00:16:43.310
Hey, hold on.

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:46.240
Getting something to eat on the way home

00:16:46.240 --> 00:16:48.210
is against school rules!

00:16:49.630 --> 00:16:51.070
Upperclassman Jikukawa!

00:16:51.460 --> 00:16:54.130
I'm sorry for doubting you!

00:16:55.580 --> 00:17:00.080
My apologies for thinking that,
once you'd put the Ring on,

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:01.450
you would lose to Kaito.

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:03.660
Well, I hope you've learned
from your mistake.

00:17:09.540 --> 00:17:12.360
Upperclassman Jikukawa, you...

00:17:12.360 --> 00:17:14.720
As soon as the Ring came off,

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:17.180
I realized what I'd wanted to know.

00:17:17.530 --> 00:17:20.100
The key to removing the Replica Ring

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:22.200
is the feeling of having lost.

00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:24.830
People are freed from the Rings

00:17:24.830 --> 00:17:26.980
when they've admitted that they've lost.

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:29.670
Huh? That's...

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:34.260
Correct. It's what we'd surmised
from our data up till now.

00:17:34.260 --> 00:17:36.950
But it was only a hypothesis.

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:39.920
I wanted to get some concrete data.

00:17:40.300 --> 00:17:42.350
And we got PLENTY of data!

00:17:42.350 --> 00:17:44.870
From when you put it on up until it came off. Right?

00:17:45.100 --> 00:17:49.150
That's why you went so far,
doin' this reckless stuff?

00:17:49.150 --> 00:17:50.710
Even keepin' US in the dark.

00:17:51.150 --> 00:17:54.210
They say it takes an ally
to dupe an enemy, right?

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:58.460
We didn't want to arouse
the Orpheus Order's suspicions.

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:04.700
Still, I forced you to be my
accomplice in this, Cubik.

00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:08.100
Thank you. And...

00:18:08.330 --> 00:18:09.290
I'm sorry.

00:18:10.370 --> 00:18:11.440
It's fine!

00:18:11.920 --> 00:18:14.000
After all, I got to see Gammon kowtow.

00:18:19.930 --> 00:18:21.730
Sure enough, this stuff is delicious.

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:33.300
Yes. We have finished compiling data

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:35.380
on the beta-test Orpheus Rings.

00:18:35.820 --> 00:18:39.510
Yes. We shall now move
to the feedback stage.

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:49.020
Congratulations on winning the election,
Miss Student Council President!

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:50.000
Victor

00:18:49.710 --> 00:18:51.710
Thank you, everyone.

00:18:55.340 --> 00:18:58.820
Now, I can protect Upperclassman Jikukawa's
student council.

00:18:58.840 --> 00:19:00.760
-dera       Chieno

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:08.520
2  Naoki Takeda
6  Shichiro Okudera

00:19:06.810 --> 00:19:08.520
Whaaaa?!

00:19:08.520 --> 00:19:12.350
Two votes? Just two votes?!

00:19:12.350 --> 00:19:15.520
Who do you think the other voter was?

00:19:16.520 --> 00:19:18.260
I have to do my best.

00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:20.650
So Upperclassman Jikukawa
won't be disappointed

00:19:20.650 --> 00:19:22.340
when he comes back.

00:19:22.700 --> 00:19:23.950
That's right.

00:19:28.490 --> 00:19:32.370
I wonder where Upperclassman
Jikukawa is right now...

00:19:32.740 --> 00:19:35.430
He's a selfish bugger, as always.

00:19:35.430 --> 00:19:37.520
He just left without sayin' anything.

00:19:38.090 --> 00:19:39.650
I, Ana, think...

00:19:41.130 --> 00:19:42.880
He'll be back soon!

00:19:44.300 --> 00:19:48.910
'Cuz he's got so many absences
that he can't graduate.

00:19:49.350 --> 00:19:50.950
When that happens, I'll teach you how

00:19:50.950 --> 00:19:52.830
to give our upperclassman
a proper kowtow.

00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:56.250
When that happens, your ass better be
doin' a kowtow, too!

00:19:59.320 --> 00:20:00.880
Kaito,

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:07.410
From Jikukawa
To Kaito

00:20:01.610 --> 00:20:04.860
Is everyone mad that I
suddenly disappeared?

00:20:04.950 --> 00:20:07.160
They may be rather surprised.

00:20:07.830 --> 00:20:12.460
I texted you thinking I could tell you,
at least, the whole truth.

00:20:13.870 --> 00:20:17.630
I think you've realized
that, at the time,

00:20:17.630 --> 00:20:20.400
I was completely possessed by the Replica Ring.

00:20:21.090 --> 00:20:25.140
My, my. That Ring really
is something else.

00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:28.480
Brain activity is increased, and puzzles

00:20:28.480 --> 00:20:31.240
can be solved faster and more profoundly.

00:20:31.970 --> 00:20:35.550
It is truly the forbidden
fruit that must not be eaten.

00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:38.780
Wearing the Orpheus Order's Ring,

00:20:38.780 --> 00:20:40.500
removed from my own perception,

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:42.950
I was once again made aware
of your incredible ability.

00:20:44.320 --> 00:20:47.660
Still, all of this was expected.

00:20:47.820 --> 00:20:50.280
I didn't mention this to Cubik,

00:20:50.280 --> 00:20:53.440
but there was something else
I wanted to investigate.

00:20:53.950 --> 00:20:56.210
The truth behind the Replica Rings.

00:21:00.290 --> 00:21:03.160
A fake can never approach the real thing.

00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:06.200
I know that all too well.

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:08.630
And yet, there is a way to

00:21:08.630 --> 00:21:10.700
approach the real thing,
one without boundaries...

00:21:11.300 --> 00:21:14.810
If a real Phi-Brain child like
yourself were to

00:21:14.810 --> 00:21:17.010
wear a Replica Ring,

00:21:17.010 --> 00:21:19.800
it would seek to become
a true Orpheus Ring.

00:21:20.520 --> 00:21:24.490
It is YOU the Replica Rings seek, Kaito.

00:21:27.660 --> 00:21:32.720
I was drawn too far into
the Ring trying to learn this,

00:21:32.720 --> 00:21:35.780
but thanks to you,
I was able to return.

00:21:36.780 --> 00:21:40.180
However, if you were to put on a Ring,

00:21:40.180 --> 00:21:42.320
who would be able to stop you?

00:21:42.880 --> 00:21:46.950
Moreover, if that is what the
Orpheus Order is after...

00:21:47.840 --> 00:21:51.750
I will leave the academy
to find the truth.

00:21:51.750 --> 00:21:55.460
This is my final mission as a member of Section Phi.

00:21:56.600 --> 00:21:59.810
Kaito. Please take care of yourself.

00:21:59.810 --> 00:22:00.970
See you.

00:22:02.730 --> 00:22:05.220
Oh, and one last thing...

00:22:06.150 --> 00:22:07.430
I was happy.

00:22:07.430 --> 00:22:09.760
To have an all-out duel with you.

00:22:10.560 --> 00:22:13.000
Thank you, Einstein.

00:22:13.870 --> 00:22:15.180
Upperclassman Jikukawa...

00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:40.050
Eiyuukidori
Playing the hero

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:44.940
Itsudatte shinjita muteki no kankaku
A sense of invincibility you always believed in

00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:51.370
Tatakatte iru no wa chikyuu no tame nanka ja nai
You're not fighting for the sake of the world or anything

00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:54.160
Motto maipeesu de
It's for a more leisurely

00:22:54.160 --> 00:22:59.230
Sou, motto shoujiki na onegai no tame
Yeah, more straightforward request

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:07.670
Nandotonaku kizutsuitemo tachiagare, hero
Even if you're wounded over and over, rise up, hero

00:23:07.670 --> 00:23:13.220
Kitto daijoubu, kimi o mamorunda
It's sure to be all right, I'll protect you

00:23:13.610 --> 00:23:17.040
Machigai da to shitemo tomarenai
Even if it's wrong, it can't be stopped

00:23:17.040 --> 00:23:20.650
Seikai ka nante wakaranai
I don't know if it's the right answer

00:23:21.550 --> 00:23:24.660
Donna toki demo original ni
No matter the situation

00:23:24.660 --> 00:23:27.400
Step o fumidashiteku
I'll take those first steps, originally

00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:30.770
Dramatic ni, mawaru sekai de
On this spinning world, I'm searching, dramatically

00:23:30.770 --> 00:23:34.430
Kiwameita wonder sagashiteru
For wonders that sparkle

00:23:35.190 --> 00:23:38.430
Boku, shijou saikou no tabi o tsuzukeyou
Me, I'll keep going on the greatest journey in history

00:23:38.430 --> 00:23:42.740
Image shite shiawase na mirai e
To the happy future I imagined

00:23:44.430 --> 00:23:46.060
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:51.380
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:51.380 --> 00:23:52.800
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:56.260
(Mirai e)
(To the future)

00:24:02.310 --> 00:24:05.440
Kaito Daimon! I have returned.

00:24:05.440 --> 00:24:09.050
I shall make you taste ignominy, despair,

00:24:09.050 --> 00:24:12.130
beautiful fear and death!

00:24:12.130 --> 00:24:12.790
I won't allow it.

00:24:12.790 --> 00:24:15.430
Y-You! Rook Banjo C-

00:24:15.430 --> 00:24:17.550
Next time, "The Devil Has Returned"

00:24:17.200 --> 00:24:26.540
The Devil Has Returned

00:24:17.550 --> 00:24:20.600
I see. This title refers to YOU.

00:24:20.600 --> 00:24:23.040
Kaito, everyone, sorry for the wait.

00:24:23.040 --> 00:24:25.710
Now then, puzzle time... Let's begin!
